{
  "uid": "pawtograder-app-business",
  "title": "Pawtograder \u00b7 App Business Metrics",
  "tags": [
    "pawtograder",
    "business"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "datasource",
        "label": "Prometheus",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus",
        "current": {},
        "hide": 0,
        "refresh": 1,
        "regex": ""
      },
      {
        "name": "class_id",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "${datasource}"
        },
        "query": "label_values(pawtograder_active_submissions_active_count, class_id)",
        "refresh": 1,
        "current": {
          "selected": false,
          "text": "All",
          "value": "$__all"
        },
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Real classes",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "pawtograder_classes_real_classes"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Active submissions (now)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 4,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(pawtograder_active_submissions_active_count{class_id=~\"$class_id\"})"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Submissions created (1h)",
      "description": "pawtograder_submissions_created_total, from the postgres_exporter custom query in charts/pawtograder/templates/monitoring.yaml. Was web_submission_created_total, which never emitted: submissions are created by the autograder-create-submission edge function and by the browser talking to PostgREST, so the web tier never observes one.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(increase(pawtograder_submissions_created_total{class_id=~\"$class_id\"}[1h]))"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Grading actions (1h)",
      "description": "pawtograder_grading_actions_total, from the postgres_exporter custom query in charts/pawtograder/templates/monitoring.yaml. Was web_grading_action_total, which never emitted: grading comments are written through a browser Supabase client in lib/TableController.ts. Sums across all three kinds; safe to do so because every kind is now a trigger-maintained event counter that never decreases (see supabase/migrations/20260904140000_grading_action_counters.sql). The earlier COUNT(*) form fell on assignment deletion and on a bulk unrelease, which Prometheus read as a counter reset and increase() rendered as a phantom burst on this stat too, not just on the by-kind panel.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(increase(pawtograder_grading_actions_total{class_id=~\"$class_id\"}[1h]))"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Open help requests",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(pawtograder_help_queue_depth_open_count{class_id=~\"$class_id\"})"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 5
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 20
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "In-progress help",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 20,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(pawtograder_help_queue_depth_in_progress_count{class_id=~\"$class_id\"})"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Submissions created / minute (by class)",
      "description": "pawtograder_submissions_created_total reads class_metrics_totals.submissions_total, a trigger-maintained insert counter, so it is uncached and monotonic. THE [5m] WINDOW IS DELIBERATE \u2014 do not shorten it. The exporter is scraped every 30s, so a [1m] window holds exactly two samples and one missed scrape blanks the panel. * 60 converts per-second back to per-minute.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "class {{class_id}}",
          "expr": "sum by(class_id)(rate(pawtograder_submissions_created_total{class_id=~\"$class_id\"}[5m])) * 60"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Grading actions / minute (by kind)",
      "description": "kind is comment (free-text), rubric_check (comment carrying a rubric_check_id) or release (a submission_reviews release event). All three come from trigger-maintained counter columns on class_metrics_totals and count ACTIONS, not surviving rows: a retracted comment, a deleted assignment and a bulk unrelease all leave the counter where it was, so none of them reads as a counter reset. THE [5m] WINDOW IS DELIBERATE \u2014 do not shorten it. The exporter is scraped every 30s, so a [1m] window holds exactly two samples and one missed scrape blanks the panel. * 60 converts per-second back to per-minute.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{kind}}",
          "expr": "sum by(kind)(rate(pawtograder_grading_actions_total{class_id=~\"$class_id\"}[5m])) * 60"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Active submissions over time (by class)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 12
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "class {{class_id}}",
          "expr": "pawtograder_active_submissions_active_count{class_id=~\"$class_id\"}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Help queue depth (open + in-progress)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 12
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "open",
          "legendFormat": "open class {{class_id}}",
          "expr": "pawtograder_help_queue_depth_open_count{class_id=~\"$class_id\"}"
        },
        {
          "refId": "ip",
          "legendFormat": "in-progress class {{class_id}}",
          "expr": "pawtograder_help_queue_depth_in_progress_count{class_id=~\"$class_id\"}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 30,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Top classes by recent activity (1h)",
      "description": "sum by(class_id) is applied to each metric BEFORE the addition. Adding the raw increase() vectors does not work: pawtograder_grading_actions_total carries a kind label that pawtograder_submissions_created_total does not, so PromQL finds no matching label sets and the panel returns empty. Both exporter queries are driven off public.classes so every class emits a zero-filled series on both sides and no class drops out of the sum.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 20
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true,
          "expr": "topk(20, sum by(class_id)(increase(pawtograder_submissions_created_total[1h])) + sum by(class_id)(increase(pawtograder_grading_actions_total[1h])))"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 40,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Autograder workflow runs",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 28
      },
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "id": 41,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Workflow runs (1h)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 29
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(web_workflow_runs_recent{class_id=~\"$class_id\", window=\"1h\"})"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 42,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Workflow error rate (1h)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 29
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(web_workflow_runs_recent{class_id=~\"$class_id\", conclusion!~\"success|skipped\", window=\"1h\"}) / clamp_min(sum(web_workflow_runs_recent{class_id=~\"$class_id\", window=\"1h\"}), 1)"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 0.05
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.15
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 43,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "P95 queue duration (1h)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 29
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "max(web_workflow_queue_seconds{class_id=~\"$class_id\", quantile=\"0.95\"})"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 60
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 300
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 44,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "P95 run duration (1h)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 29
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "max(web_workflow_run_seconds{class_id=~\"$class_id\", quantile=\"0.95\"})"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 180
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 600
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 50,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Workflow runs by conclusion (1h windows)",
      "description": "Each series is a sliding count of completed workflow runs by GitHub conclusion. `success`/`skipped` are the healthy paths; everything else (failure, cancelled, timed_out, neutral, action_required, unknown) is a failure mode.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 33
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{conclusion}}",
          "expr": "sum by(conclusion)(web_workflow_runs_recent{class_id=~\"$class_id\", window=\"1h\"})"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 51,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Workflow error rate over time (1h windows, by class)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 33
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "class {{class_id}}",
          "expr": "sum by(class_id)(web_workflow_runs_recent{class_id=~\"$class_id\", conclusion!~\"success|skipped\", window=\"1h\"}) / clamp_min(sum by(class_id)(web_workflow_runs_recent{class_id=~\"$class_id\", window=\"1h\"}), 1)"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 0.05
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.15
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 60,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Workflow queue duration (P50/P95/P99) by class",
      "description": "Time from workflow_runs.requested_at to in_progress_at. Spikes here mean GitHub Actions runner backlog or grader image pull/start delays.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 41
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "p50",
          "legendFormat": "p50 class {{class_id}}",
          "expr": "web_workflow_queue_seconds{class_id=~\"$class_id\", quantile=\"0.5\"}"
        },
        {
          "refId": "p95",
          "legendFormat": "p95 class {{class_id}}",
          "expr": "web_workflow_queue_seconds{class_id=~\"$class_id\", quantile=\"0.95\"}"
        },
        {
          "refId": "p99",
          "legendFormat": "p99 class {{class_id}}",
          "expr": "web_workflow_queue_seconds{class_id=~\"$class_id\", quantile=\"0.99\"}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "min": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 61,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Workflow run duration (P50/P95) by class",
      "description": "Time from in_progress_at to completed_at \u2014 actual grader execution.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 41
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "p50",
          "legendFormat": "p50 class {{class_id}}",
          "expr": "web_workflow_run_seconds{class_id=~\"$class_id\", quantile=\"0.5\"}"
        },
        {
          "refId": "p95",
          "legendFormat": "p95 class {{class_id}}",
          "expr": "web_workflow_run_seconds{class_id=~\"$class_id\", quantile=\"0.95\"}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "min": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 70,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Workflow errors by category in the last 1h",
      "description": "web_workflow_errors_recent, grouped by a CLOSED error category, not by workflow_run_error.name. The name column is the student-visible sentence \u2014 free text capped only at 500 characters, and several producers embed a commit sha in it \u2014 so as a Prometheus label it minted a new series per distinct message and Prometheus keeps every series it has ever seen. The categories come from workflow_run_error.data (error_type / type) via metrics_workflow_errors_by_category and can only be file_too_large, submission_too_large, empty_submission, after_due_date, missing_grader_result, grader or other. For the actual messages, use the instructor Workflow Errors page or query workflow_run_error directly \u2014 the detail is in the database and the logs, deliberately not in a label.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 49
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true,
          "expr": "topk(15, web_workflow_errors_recent{class_id=~\"$class_id\", window=\"1h\"})"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 80,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Web tier (Next.js server)",
      "description": "Produced by prom-client inside the pawtograder-web pods and scraped from /api/metrics \u2014 the same target as the workflow row above, which is why these live here rather than on their own dashboard. NONE of these panels honour $class_id: the route and rpc labels are hardcoded patterns with no class dimension, deliberately, because a per-course label on a 12-bucket histogram is unbounded cardinality driven by a public URL. Everything is summed across pods; break out by pod in Explore if you suspect one replica.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 58
      },
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "id": 81,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "SSR Supabase RPC p95 (by rpc)",
      "description": "95th percentile of the server-side Supabase calls wrapped by timeRpc (lib/ssrUtils.ts, lib/ssr-course-dashboard.ts, lib/lti/*). This is the closest thing to \"how slow is an RSC page render\" that exists: RSC renders themselves have no instrumentation seam short of middleware, and middleware is the Edge runtime where prom-client does not run. Expect this to be SPARSE \u2014 most business reads in this app go browser to PostgREST and never touch the server.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 59
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{rpc}}",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by(le,rpc)(rate(web_supabase_rpc_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])))"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 82,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "SSR Supabase RPC errors / sec (by rpc, code)",
      "description": "code is a Postgres SQLSTATE, the literal \"throw\" when the call rejected rather than returning an error envelope, or \"unknown\". It is never an error message: normalizeRpcErrorCode() in lib/metrics.ts collapses anything not matching /^[0-9A-Z]{5}$/, because a PostgREST message embeds the offending value and would be unbounded cardinality on a counter.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 59
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{rpc}} / {{code}}",
          "expr": "sum by(rpc,code)(rate(web_supabase_rpc_errors_total[5m]))"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 83,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "API route p95 latency (by route)",
      "description": "95th percentile per route handler under app/api. route is the literal parameterized App Router pattern hardcoded per file (e.g. /api/calendar/[course_id]) \u2014 never the request path. /api/tunnel (Sentry, high volume, no diagnostic value) and /api/metrics (the self-scrape) are deliberately not instrumented.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 67
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{route}}",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by(le,route)(rate(web_http_request_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])))"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 84,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "API route requests / sec (by route, status class)",
      "description": "status is bucketed to 2xx/4xx/5xx rather than the exact code. The exact code is in Sentry and the access log; carrying it here would roughly double the http family for no signal any panel reads.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 67
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
